If they did not seek grant of land, did they have right to challenge the order of grant in favour of seventh respondent being interested persons, is the question that obviously arises in the backdrop of entire scenario and the decisions of the Supreme Court in the cases of AYAAUBKHAN NOORKHAN PATHAN vs STATE OF MAHARASHTRA AND OTHERS [(2013) 4 SCC 465];
JASBHAI MOTIBHAI DESAI vs ROSHAN KUMAR, HAJI BASHIR AHMED AND OTHERS [(1976)
1 SCC 671]; ANAND SHARADCHANDRA OKA vs UNIVERSITY OF MUMBAI AND OTHERS [(2008) 5 SCC 217] and Dr. SATYANARAYANA SINHA vs M/S. S.LAL AND COMPANY [(1973) 2 SCC 696] and a decision of this court in the case of S.M.KANNAPPA AUTOMOBILES vs KOLADAMATT MAHASAMSTHANA [(2020) 8 KANT LJ 1]; which are cited by Sri. Ashok Harnahalli.
